From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:32:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build the lazy camera provider in every product

The lazy provider binary is disabled unless the soong config variable gch.use_lazy_hal is set, and
that variable disables the eager provider instead, which the stock emulated camera APEX packages. A
product that installs the lazy provider cannot set the variable without leaving that APEX with a
disabled dependency.

Build the lazy provider's defaults in every product. The eager provider is built as before (unless
the variable is set), and a product installs the one it names.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 common/hal/aidl_service/Android.bp | 7 +------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/common/hal/aidl_service/Android.bp b/common/hal/aidl_service/Android.bp
index 55cffa9ec6c0766f75ec8c368b66d926adef079c..ce3d2fe915b0604a064edd7cd51be5078d62570c 100644
--- a/common/hal/aidl_service/Android.bp
+++ b/common/hal/aidl_service/Android.bp
@@ -42,12 +42,7 @@ gch_lazy_hal_cc_defaults {
 
 gch_lazy_hal_cc_defaults {
     name: "camera_service_lazy_hal_defaults",
-    enabled: false,
-    soong_config_variables: {
-        use_lazy_hal: {
-            enabled: true,
-        },
-    },
+    enabled: true,
 }
 
 // Exported for use in vendor/google/services/LyricCameraHAL/src/
